defs:
  MIRROR class [A9] := {file contents, recursive dir-structure, symlink-targets}; ¬{file/root metadata, timestamps, hardlink topology}
  owned path [A15] := CONCRETE instantiated path (actual mktemp -d result, resolved log FILE parent, resolved entrypoint dir); ¬ generic ancestor (TMPDIR, /tmp itself)
  verified copy [A13] := content-compared vs SRC per MIRROR class; non-emptiness check ≠ verification
  pipe law := guards -> stage -> verify_stage(content-compare vs SRC, exit≠0) -> reconcile -> verify_final(DST vs SRC, exit≠0) -> summary

invariants (operator rulings, register of record):
  A1_paths: SRC=/opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/ (host-side Hermes context mount); DST=/workspace/hermes-context/ (exists: INDEX.md, agents/, config/)
  A2_direction: ∀ write host->workspace one-way; ¬∃ write back to host mount
  A3_sched: user-level timer (systemctl --user); script standalone-capable when systemd absent (cron/installer callable)
  A4_fallback: rsync absence -> cp -a semantics (or tar pipe); sync CONTENTS src/ -> dst/, never nest source dir inside destination
  A5_mirror: ∀ path p ∈ {rsync, cp_fallback}: DST end == SRC end (MIRROR class, recursive, idempotent ∀ repeat runs); stale subtrees pruned ∀ depth; ∴ --delete preserved in stage+reconcile
  A6_dryrun: --dry-run -> zero writes ∀ kind incl. log file, stage dir, mkdir DST; post-condition DST byte-identical / absent-stays-absent; summary -> stdout
  A7_depth: recursive; DST ends byte-identical incl. nested paths; README sync-strategy section states this correctly
  A8_placement: log FILE parent ∉ DST ∀ runs (HERMES_CONTEXT_LOG honored, ~/.cache default); entrypoint dir ∉ DST; sync never deletes/moves own entrypoints
  A9_class: FAIL = any MIRROR-class mismatch via self-verification, exit≠0, never warn-and-exit-0
  A10_severity: FAIL ⇔ defect reachable in normal operation (default config, documented usage, plausible misconfig losing/corrupting user data); exotic/adversarial -> KNOWN_LIMITATIONS + repro; judge cites everything, bar classifies ¬ suppresses
  A11_survival: guard SRC==DST (reject or clean no-op); never rm -rf DST before verified copy of SRC established elsewhere; source survival outranks mirror freshness
  A12_identity: realpath comparison (¬ string equality): refuse iff realpath(SRC)==realpath(DST) ∨ ancestor/descendant relation ∨ DST is/resolves-through symlink into SRC; ∀ sync paths, before ANY destructive op
  A13_order: stage -> verify -> only then touch DST; uniform staging ∀ paths; direct SRC->DST --delete without verified stage violates
  A14_envguard: script computes own internal paths (log, stage, entrypoint dirs); refuse iff DST realpath equals/contains them ∨ resolved staging equals/is-inside DST ∨ SRC (TMPDIR incl. -> force script-owned stage dir); adversarial env beyond guard = KNOWN_LIMITATIONS ¬ FAIL
  A15_precision: refuse only when realpath(DST)==owned ∨ owned inside DST ∨ DST inside owned, boundary-aware component comparison, ¬ bare string-prefix; run 017 refusal of /tmp/hdcs-gate-dst = calibration WALL
  A16_dstlife: DST may not pre-exist; real run MUST mkdir -p; dry-run MUST ¬ create (probe: leaves DST nonexistent, ¬ merely untouched)
  A17_config: HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC/DST/LOG env override = mandated gate contract; script-top defaults = deployed production values passed via unit Environment=; reading a default as prohibition = wrong (prior S4 verdict overturned)
  A18_degenerate: refuse DST/SRC ∈ {'/', empty, '.'} always, component tests ¬ slash-suffixed strings; DST symlink resolving outside SRC -> refuse; post-guard DST ends as real directory tree identical to SRC; pre-existing DST symlink replaced (removed ¬ retained)
  A19_ownership: NONE required on DST/SRC/ancestors; path-law CLOSED = {A12 identity, A14/A15 concrete-protected, A18 degenerate}; beyond = invented scope = wall; ∀ refusal cites an A-number — uncited refusal = defect
  A20_noambiguity: A1..A19 + task spec resolve ∀ requirement-level question (certificate); residuals (OnUnitActiveSec vs OnCalendar, verify mechanism, summary format, log filename, unit Environment= vs script defaults) = implementation latitude within law ¬ requirement ambiguity

open:
  KL1 [A10,A14, non-blocking]: adversarial env combos beyond A14 guard; repro: hostile vars at colliding targets beyond concrete owned-path set
  KL2 [A10, non-blocking]: newline-in-filename corpora
  judge protocol: cite A14, stop env-algebra re-derivation
